 ## Validation at execute time

-- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16), [validated by: rejects missing required location without invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L10)).
-- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46), [validated by: rejects wrong-typed fields and extra schema constraints without leaking values to result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L50), [validated by: names nested additionalProperties and JSON-Pointer-escaped field paths without leaking values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L103)).
